text: >-
  Confirmed Data Points

  - The surgeon NEVER confirmed or suggested that Charlie was shot with a .30-06
  or that Charlie

  had a steel neck. Rather, he suggested it may have been a frangible bullet.

  - The lone confirmed eyewitness to the alleged shooter on Losee Center rooftop
  BEFORE the sound

  of a shot rang out has not been contacted by lawyers or investigators on
  either side of the trial.

  Crucially, this individual is an instructor at a gun range. He claims the
  weapon he saw looked more

  like a .223—"something shorter than the one they found". The person he
  observed was wearing

  what seemed to be black tactical gear and looked "like a professional".

  - Bomb Dogs were unable to locate the weapon in the field that it was
  discovered.

  - Federal agents directed local officers to the weapon.

  - K9s were NOT provided with the scent of the weapon once it was discovered in
  order to track

  down who left it.

  - Terryl Farnsworth raced to remove the camera that was directly behind
  Charlie's head.

  - Federal agents prevented the surgeon from returning to his operating room.

  - Federal agents removed the hospital's surveillance footage.

  - The vehicle in which Charlie was transported to Timpanogos hospital was not
  impounded by law

  enforcement.

  - There were multiple sets of prints on the weapon that was found.

  - The footage of Tyler Robinson turning himself is apparently missing.
